{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule","id":472636,"title":"Changing Tribe - What is the Rule?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-08T06:44:34-07:00","id":472636,"title":"Changing Tribe - What is the Rule?","content":"Hello, everybody. <br /> <br /> I\u00b4m having a problem about the rule to change from a tribe to another.<br /> <br /> During game, when you change tribe, you lost a renown and gain another?<br /> <br /> In the character creation, you pick a renown dot from the tribe. So, this renown &quot;belongs&quot; to the tribe, not the character. If you change from Hunter in Darkness (Honor) to Storm Lords (Purity), did you change a renown to another? Or you simply lost the renown?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:49:59-07:00","id":472658,"title":"","content":"Neither. Your renown stays the same. Remember that Renown is based on your character's previous deeds and actions. During your initiation into one Tribe, you probably did something awesome that gained you that renown. After you perform the Initiation to join the new tribe you <i>may</i> have gained a new renown of that Tribe's type, but you would have to spend experience to get it and it would only count if it's better than whatever you did to obtain your current score in the relevant renown (naturally if you have no dots in a renown you don't have to do too much).<br /> <br /> But yeah, you don't lose renown for leaving a tribe and you don't necessarily gain renown for joining a tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T07:02:58-07:00","id":472667,"title":"","content":"My doubt came because if Ghost Wolves don\u00b4t receive the renown of a tribe, it\u00b4s because this renown it\u00b4s not acquired by deeds. Instead, it\u00b4s a gift from the Firstborn. <br /> <br /> But that\u00b4s just a interpretation, since the book it\u00b4s not clear enough about that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:15:13-07:00","id":472786,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I don't actually know why they punish Ghost Wolves that way, when Renown is based on Deeds. Is there some reason they can't have done some Deed regardless of having a Tribe or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:18:59-07:00","id":472792,"title":"","content":"The tribal renown you get probably represents the deed done as an initiation into the tribe, or done by the character then seen by the tribe, which made them try and recruit the character. Ghost wolves, on the other hand, haven't done that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:32:10-07:00","id":472820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=472786#post472786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I don't actually know why they punish Ghost Wolves that way, when Renown is based on Deeds. Is there some reason they can't have done some Deed regardless of having a Tribe or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea behind Ghost Wolves is that they have actively avoided joining a Tribe whereas everyone else has actively pursued the relationship. Just look at the Wolf-Blooded Merit for being tied to the &quot;Ghost Wolf Tribe&quot;: it's about being actively non-commital. As such, Ghost Wolves simply haven't done thing necessary for that extra Renown dot (much as nofather said).<br /> <br /> As to why they &quot;punish&quot; them, I think there's two reasons. First is that being in a Tribe is supposed to have benefits. If you could take equivalent benefits without joining the Tribe, would being in the Tribe really have benefits? In a lot of games, flexibility is considered a big benefit in and of itself, so having two free-choice Renown dots without any restricting oath or vow would, from some perspectives, make Ghost Wolves the go-to choice. <br /> And that's not at all what the game is about. It's about finding your place in the larger group while struggling with a nature that wants to say you're the best there is. The strength of the pack is the wolf and the strength of the wolf is the pack. As much as you might like to be a loner, it's not good for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:23:31-07:00","id":473329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=472786#post472786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I don't actually know why they punish Ghost Wolves that way, when Renown is based on Deeds. Is there some reason they can't have done some Deed regardless of having a Tribe or not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the same way. The only explanation that make sense to me, it\u00b4s that the renown it\u00b4s a gift from the Firstborn, as the gifts. So, when you leave or enter a tribe, you will be gived or removed from a dot. <br /> <br /> That\u00b4s why the Ghost Wolves don\u00b4t receive anything (nor renown, or gifts). Because no one will give that.<br /> <br /> In char creation, under tribe, say that &quot;Each tribe has an associated Renown. Mark a dot in that Renown.&quot;. For me, the renown it\u00b4s associated (and belongs) to the tribe. Not to the char.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:29:11-07:00","id":473334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=472792#post472792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tribal renown you get probably represents the deed done as an initiation into the tribe, or done by the character then seen by the tribe, which made them try and recruit the character. Ghost wolves, on the other hand, haven't done that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But in Tribes say &quot;Remember, unlike auspice, your character chooses her tribe. Generally, characters align relatively closely to their tribe expectations.&quot; <br /> <br /> You aren\u00b4t recruited. You choose your tribe by will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:30:13-07:00","id":473335,"title":"","content":"Tribe's or not, It's carved into their soul now and there's fuck all you can do about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:51:59-07:00","id":473380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prelks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=473334#post473334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren\u00b4t recruited. You choose your tribe by will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't mean you just want really hard and become one. Or that there can't be an initiation, or recruitment. A werewolf might think they're hard and really belong in the Storm Lords, but the Bone Shadows have been watching them and know that that's just bluster and he'd really fit in better with them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T23:02:06-07:00","id":473912,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised to see something like this covered in a supplement relatively soon. If/when the Bale Hounds get their write up I can see this being included.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms 