have to go through initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:37:03-07:00","id":474856,"title":"","content":"Tried to join a Sorority once.... Wouldn't let me in for some reason. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Some of those initiations looked.... interesting indeed...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:21:30-07:00","id":476007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=474793#post474793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lore of the Forsaken covers this in some detail.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will read them. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:22:35-07:00","id":476008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=474811#post474811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also chose to join a fraternity or a sorority. Doesn't mean you don't have to go through initiation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Make sense... But if you live a fraternity, they rip you off from the benefits, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5595-prelks","name":"Prelks","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:33:12-07:00","id":476022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prelks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=476008#post476008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sense... But if you live a fraternity, they rip you off from the benefits, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you leave a fraternity you can't live with them anymore (lose the benefit), but you'll always have done the things they had you do when they were making you join. If part of the process of joining up was to jump in a lake and sing at the top of your lungs while naked, once you leave you still will have jupmed in a lake and sung at the top of your lungs while naked.<br /> Renown is about the Awesome Things You Did. Maybe someone made you do it. Maybe the fact that you did it made people take notice of you. Either way, if you've got a dot of Renown, you Did That Thing, and nobody can take that away from you.<br /> <br /> Edit: so I have other threads elsewhere about Renown as a Totem benefit, but I tend to call that &quot;effective Renown&quot;. I.e. being with the totem helps you in ways akin to having Renown without actually having it. The Tribal dot you get at creation is a real Renown dot. You got it because you did something, not because someone is holding you up.<br /> <br /> Take my character for example: He's an Ithauer Bone Shadow, so he starts with 2 Wisdom. By my story, he got the first dot simply by asking for it. That might not seem like much, but successfully supplicating a Lune is a reasonably serious act of Wisdom. The second one he got while in training under his mom's Bone Shadow packmate; he helped him bind a fairly strong spirit into a Fetish. It was a big feat, but he wasn't the primary actor. He was, however, an actor in the process. <br /> If, for some reason, the Rahu in my pack someday convinces him that Hunters in Darkness are a better fit for him (not the case but this is a hypothetical), when he leaves the Bone Shadows, he still will have done all the things he did to get his Wisdom Renown dots, and thus will take them along. Before he gets too far with the HiD, though, he will have had to have done somthing to demonstrate his Purity. Otherwise he's really not a good fit for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 04-10-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:37:13-07:00","id":476026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prelks</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=476008#post476008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make sense... But if you live a fraternity, they rip you off from the benefits, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and if you leave your Tribe you no longer get the tribe's benefit when you perform the Sacred Hunt Rite, and you no longer get the cost break on their Tribal Gifts. But if you get your frat's name tattooed on your arm, they can't really make you get it removed if you leave. That's what Renown is, it's a tattoo on your spirit. They literally can't take it away from you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T13:05:38-07:00","id":476220,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for the answers..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/472636-changing-tribe-what-is-the-rule?p=476026#post476026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, and if you leave your Tribe you no longer get the tribe's benefit when you perform the Sacred Hunt Rite, and you no longer get the cost break on their Tribal Gifts. But if you get your frat's name tattooed on your arm, they can't really make you get it removed if you leave. That's what Renown is, it's a tattoo on your spirit. They literally can't take it away from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>They 